{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T01:16:28.322Z","author":"codex","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"69d1128247c162375b1cf4c6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-github-j3pn"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Closeout PR title and summary must match the plan's actions"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The merged-PR closeout workflow always titles its PR 'chore(pm): close items delivered by merged pull requests' and its summary claims verified closure, even when the plan holds no close action (example: unbraind/pm-web#354 held only skip, refuse and needs_review entries). When the plan has no close actions, the PR title and summary must be review-only ('record merged-PR closeout review candidates'), state that no items were closed, and give per-action counts; closure wording appears only when at least one close action exists. The PR body counts every action (close, skip, refuse, needs_review) derived from the same plan JSON the run wrote."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["gh:unbraind/pm-github#270"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-23T01:16:28.322Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T01:16:28.322Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"9f63f40b24a37b021aae39b6b5f7a59c207b6c790f3735e96e77b22c83864dad","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"6716b1055663